The rdz source package bundles one third-party library: Zstandard, compiled
into rdz.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Zstandard (src/vendor/zstd/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/facebook/zstd
Release:   v1.5.7 (commit f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99)
License:   BSD-3-Clause (zstd is dual-licensed BSD and GPLv2; rdz uses it
           under the BSD license). The notice is reproduced verbatim in
           src/vendor/zstd/LICENSE.

  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. All rights reserved.

src/vendor/zstd/zstd.c is the release's own amalgamation script
(build/single_file_libs/combine.py) run over the release's lib/ sources with
rdz's input file tools/vendor/zstd-in.c, which is upstream's zstd-in.c without
ZSTD_MULTITHREAD and without the dictionary builder. zstd.h, zstd_errors.h and
LICENSE are the release's files. No source is modified; the build sets
ZSTDLIB_VISIBLE and ZSTDERRORLIB_VISIBLE empty so that no zstd symbol is
exported. tools/vendor/manifest.tsv records the archive checksum, and
tools/vendor/verify checks the vendored files against
tools/vendor/checksums.sha256.
